{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1357576-white-elephant-for-orukan-a-menagerie-of-monsters-of-the-western-seas","id":1357576,"title":"[White Elephant for Orukan] A Menagerie of Monsters of the Western Seas!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-29T11:23:11-08:00","id":1357576,"title":"[White Elephant for Orukan] A Menagerie of Monsters of the Western Seas!","content":"As you asked for some monsters of the West, I decided to give you a buffet of options!. I hope you like them!<br /> <br /> Strange Monstrosities of the Western Oceans<br /> <br /> <br /> Grate Forks, the Tourist Trap of Coral<br /> <br /> <br /> Not to be confused with the similarly named city in the Scavenger Lands, this city is not a city of gods, but rather a city of many spirits, namely the Spirits of Greed and Vice. Grate Forks is a ramshackle city of endless bazaars, with only the Imperial Hotel and the Scarlet Honey's Tavern being wholly new buildings not constructed of shipwrecks. These markets sell everything from authenticated relics from Immaculate Saints, to really, truly actual pixie dust, made of real pixies, and salvation on demand, delivered by the gods of the Azure Bathhouse themselves. Of course, most of these are fake, but some authentic treasures sometimes slip through the cracks of the operation laid out within the city. You see, the city and everyone in it are all owned by one person; the Changing Moon Huckster and general con artist, Golden Crescent. An imposing woman, suitable for her sun bear totem and her ruthless business acumen. She doesn't tolerate independent traders in her city, extracting levies from those who seek to ply their wares either through threats or by force from her army of hired goons. Such is her plan, to artificially create a trade hub and tourist trap which efficiently and diligently removes gold from newcomers, providing them with pleasant experiences all while they don't suspect the rampant robbery occurring.<br /> <br /> <br /> Golden Crescent in her human form is a tall Eastern woman with a carefully coiffed mane of strawberry blonde hair, fond of wearing eastern robes rather than the usual fashions of the West. Her totem animal is a handsome sun bear, with silver marking her fur thanks to her tattoos. She favors manipulation and guile in her dealings with people, even going so far as to cut potential assassins down using her fighting spirit to cow them into defeat. However, should a potential opponent impress her, she will seek a more traditional diplomatic tack. When pressed, she will reveal a mastery of the Eyes of Heaven Style of martial arts, adding credence to the stories of her punching out the hearts of those who failed to pay her their dues.<br /> <br /> The Albatross Kissed by the Rime-bound Seas<br /> <br /> <br /> Dangers abound on the high seas, but none are more enigmatic than the danger of a terror spoken about only in hushed whispers by mariners. A buccaneer of Caul, infamous through her exploits against the Imperial Fleets of House Nellens, this scoundrel suddenly vanished, reappearing as a spectral monster. Legends spoke of a disastrous attempt to conquer the White Sea, to even being marooned in the Wyld-Seas, driving her mad, but one can be sure Creation's seas are not safe so long as she plies her trade. The Albatross, the Rime-Kissed Goddess of Death. Siakal Incarnate. These are her names and more. A pirate flying a banner of a single blade slashing through a single seabird, her ship a gigantic hulk the likes of which is almost unbelievable in the modern era. Even so, despite its mass, the ship is as nimble as a petite cutter, making her capable of even outrunning and outfighting even valuable essence-powered ships. Her weaponry few can say with certainty, but this monstrosity is spoken of possessing weapons which hurl vast gouts of flame, large mirrors which focus the Sun's rays into a beam of pure death, or even boxes which open to reveal the spirits of mariners the crew caught, releasing them to terrorize and possess her living victims. Few can withstand this onslaught, let alone have hopes of fighting back, as comparable vessels often only catch this ship's sails as it slinks away over the horizon.<br /> Personally, she appears as a coquettish woman in her forties, with graying auburn hair, but with the vigor to scramble up the rigging in a few seconds. Usually wearing the crimson jackets of defeated Realm naval officers, she has quite the impressive collection of gathered medals, apparently a marksman first class three time over, and recipient of two of the Crimson Majesty's Royal Order Star twice. For personal weapons, she favors an odd weapon not usually seen; a sort of firewand which fires tiny black iron balls with extreme force. This weapon, that she boasts she found in the half-mad dreams of dead gods, is as poisonous as it is unnerving as those struck weakn, sicken and die within hours unless the ball is removed from their person. Her other favored weapon is somehow even more insidious, an elegant black and silver steel cutlass whose crossguard is the skull of an unknown avian. If it strikes another, that person is immediately struck with the most horrible of luck. Everything goes wrong for them: they trip over their feet. Poor actions on the parts of their fellows which ordinarily would cause no trouble, like spilled water, or shoddily stowed firedust, become deadly obstacles. The only known cure to this malady was a careful concotion of four leafe clovers, gold, and powerful catfish from the North, this is a dark curse to impose.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lord Corvolo, Patron of Whales, Master of Cetaceans.<br /> <br /> <br /> More a denizen of the White Sea, the God of Whales can be spotted in the west, though, as his charges swim across the gamut of the vast seas therein. Never out of the company of his attendant, Basileus, Lord of the Horned Megauniwhals, he ensures the Law of the Pod is observed by his charges, and their natures are observed. Despite being a god of the Convention of Nature, he also is well-displaced towards the newly returned Lawgivers, relieved that their return has halted some of the predations of the remaining Sirens and Leviathans, restoring the balance between Humanity and Nature on the high seas.<br /> Appearing as a jet-black orca in his usual form, he also is known to appear as a Haslanti man in jet-black furs, a deep shadow cast over his face seemingly at all angles. Despite this foreboding appearance, Corvolo is a congenial fellow, helping Solars and Lunars as he can, even sending some on great trials to find some ancient treasure. Being the Lord of Whales, he has memories stretching back to the Dawn of Time, and with no need for treasure, he merely keeps such information aside when it could become useful.<br /> <br /> Delph Bacchus, Hallowed Dolphin Knight, Peer of the Scarlet Dragon Prince<br /> <br /> <br /> Out of the Beast Knights, those cataphractoi arrayed by the unshaped Scarlet Dragon Prince, to annihilate Creation with Creation's own weapons, none are more feared than the Dolphin Knight. Appearing as a skinny western man in a slick silver body tights with a knife-edge cap unpon his brow, he is always smiling, and those who know him dread this grin more than his anger. Delph is a creature of absolute freedom and passions, who sees no inhibitions to his pursuits as the best of Life. Freely loving those around him, even if they desperately plead him to not do so, freely stealing and mocking others with his flute-like voice. The other Beast Knights say nothing to this deplorable behavior, as he is a superb warrior who humiliates and ruins Creation's Warriors readily and often, even if he terrorizes his fellows just as often. The only check to this onslaught is the Housecat Knight, Calico Whiskins, whose inexplicable powers bedevil even the raucous Dolphin Knight. Thus, to those who seem him grinning as he approaches, be afraid and flee. The Dolphin's company is not one you wish!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}